event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2349,"item_id":"fc_0a05c72cce1c7da3016adb5788ac88819196fc0c6db58de3b9","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Original exercise asks compact E⊆R^(d−1), while approved frozen target explicitly adds nonemptiness and recasts dimension parameter as n≥0. This is an explicit user-approved test-target change, not a hidden hypothesis, and the full frozen/spec targets agree. However the graph target P itself is only “dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1” with no binders, n/E domains, nonemptiness, compactness, I=[0,1], ambient metric or metric correspondence. It is not the full specified target. Edge cases are discussed in S001/S003, including n=0 and D=0; empty E is appropriately excluded by H001. Product Euclidean metric is asserted, but the global target statement does not encode it.\",\"locations\":[\"problem.md:3\",\"frozen-target.md:7-17\",\"source-context.md:12-21\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{\"D001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"D001 only names pinned Mathlib Lebesgue volume on R; it introduces no extra property or hidden theorem. It is used in the slicing calculation and linked volume results.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/0\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/ν\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:86\"]}},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature evidence agrees with official theorem: implicit EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace, BorelSpace, set and NNReal exponent; strict coercion exponent below dimH yields Hausdorff measure top. The file's proof uses the dimension supremum and measure monotonicity. Actual use binds E and an exponent 0<s<D as stated.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/2/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:107-118\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Probe full telescope and official source agree: measurable carrier, measure, Countable β, ENNReal summand functions and AEMeasurable for every index. Its S002 application names ℕ and the restricted Lebesgue measure and explains measurability of each interval indicator times constant.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/3/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360-371\"]},\"M003\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Signature/source agree: Borel extended metric structures, set, NNReal exponent, dimH(A)<↑d implies measure zero. Application uses exponent above dimH(E), and above dimH(F) in the upper estimate.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M003/0/sources/M003\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/5/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/2\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:107-108\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:130-135\"]},\"M004\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature includes two EMetricSpace instances, NNReal K and LipschitzWith K f, concluding image dimension ≤ source dimension. Projection binding and Euclidean distance estimate match this contract.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M004/0/sources/M004\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/6/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/3\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:44-52\"]},\"M005\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature requires NormedAddCommGroup, NormedSpace R, FiniteDimensional R and nonempty interior. The interval application supplies the usual real structures, finrank one and interior witness.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M005/0/sources/M005\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/7/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/4\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:54-57\"]},\"M008\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official formula and full evidence agree on real exponent, EMetricSpace, measurable/Borel structures, positive ENNReal scale, Nat-indexed covers, and supremum over nonempty-set witnesses of diameter power. The prose restatement conveys these ingredients and the exact unnormalized cover infimum used for content. The declared source is a theorem formula, not a definition masquerading as a result.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M008/0/sources/M008\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/8/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/5\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/10\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Hausdorff.lean:547-552\"]},\"M009\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem has implicit measurable-space and measure structures and pointwise function inequality; these are represented accurately. Its use integrates an asserted pointwise inequality for ENNReal functions.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M009/0/sources/M009\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/9/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/6\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:\"]},\"M010\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem additionally requires MeasurableSet s and returns indicator integral equal to c times measure s. The two applications identify [0,1] and J_i∩[0,1] as measurable and constants in ENNReal.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M010/0/sources/M010\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/10/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/7\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/13\"]},\"M011\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official Real.volume_Icc has arbitrary real endpoints and returns volume(Icc a b)=ofReal(b−a), agreeing with restatement, including reversed endpoints under ofReal convention. Applications use 0,1 and enclosing endpoints.\",\"locations\":[\"si