ted with a covering/length property, and ν definition appends a mass calculation). S001/S002/S003 are argument segments within this single R and are not independent accepted proofs; their assertions must be supported by the complete argument. The supplied task excludes per-inference packet replay, which is not represented here as performed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/13\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/22\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\",\"spec.json:/full_target\"],\"finding\":\"Output statement omits the universal binders and hypotheses/domain/metric conventions of the full target; therefore the producer's output is not exactly the specified theorem.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/13\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"J_i is declared as a definition that already chooses an open interval containing B_i with a prescribed length bound. This carries a nontrivial existence/construction assertion without a separate proof or legitimate witness basis; a definition cannot supply it.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"The ν definition includes the theorem-like calculation ν(R)=volume([0,1])=1, rather than defining ν alone and deriving its mass from M011 and the restriction definition.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"The application of the slicing inequality to arbitrary δ-cover is not justified in the argument: C_s(E,δ) is an infimum of sums over countable covers, whereas the sets A_i obtained by slicing at t must be shown to form an admissible cover with the requisite scale and their costs bounded by the corresponding indicators. The text asserts this pointwise but does not fully formalize the dependence of the admissible cover on t or the infimum comparison. This is a missing proof step in the displayed NL0 argument.\"}]}}"}

