volume on R; it introduces no extra property or hidden theorem. It is used in the slicing calculation and linked volume results.\",\"locations\":[\"spec.json:/definitions/0\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/ν\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:86\"]}},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature evidence agrees with official theorem: implicit EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace, BorelSpace, set and NNReal exponent; strict coercion exponent below dimH yields Hausdorff measure top. The file's proof uses the dimension supremum and measure monotonicity. Actual use binds E and an exponent 0<s<D as stated.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/2/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:107-118\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Probe full telescope and official source agree: measurable carrier, measure, Countable β, ENNReal summand functions and AEMeasurable for every index. Its S002 application names ℕ and the restricted Lebesgue measure and explains measurability of each interval indicator times constant.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/3/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360-371\"]},\"M003\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Signature/source agree: Borel extended metric structures, set, NNReal exponent, dimH(A)<↑d implies measure zero. Application uses exponent above dimH(E), and above dimH(F) in the upper estimate.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M003/0/sources/M003\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/5/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/2\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:107-108\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:130-135\"]},\"M004\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature includes two EMetricSpace instances, NNReal K and LipschitzWith K f, concluding image dimension ≤ source dimension. Projection binding and Euclidean distance estimate match this contract.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M004/0/sources/M004\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/6/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/3\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:44-52\"]},\"M005\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature requires NormedAddCommGroup, NormedSpace R, FiniteDimensional R and nonempty interior. The interval application supplies the usual real structures, finrank one and interior witness.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M005/0/sources/M005\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/7/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/4\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:54-57\"]},\"M008\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official formula and full evidence agree on real exponent, EMetricSpace, measurable/Borel structures, positive ENNReal scale, Nat-indexed covers, and supremum over nonempty-set witnesses of diameter power. The prose restatement conveys these ingredients and the exact unnormalized cover infimum used for content. The declared source is a theorem formula, not a definition masquerading as a result.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M008/0/sources/M008\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/8/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/5\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/10\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Hausdorff.lean:547-552\"]},\"M009\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem has implicit measurable-space and measure structures and pointwise function inequality; these are represented accurately. Its use integrates an asserted pointwise inequality for ENNReal functions.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M009/0/sources/M009\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/9/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/6\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:\"]},\"M010\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem additionally requires MeasurableSet s and returns indicator integral equal to c times measure s. The two applications identify [0,1] and J_i∩[0,1] as measurable and constants in ENNReal.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M010/0/sources/M010\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/10/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/7\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/13\"]},\"M011\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official Real.volume_Icc has arbitrary real endpoints and returns volume(Icc a b)=ofReal(b−a), agreeing with restatement, including reversed endpoints under ofReal convention. Applications use 0,1 and enclosing endpoints.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M011/0/sources/M011\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/11/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/8\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/12\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:85-86\"]},\"M012\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem has Borel extended metric structures, NNReal d and non-top Hausdorff measure premise, yielding dimH≤↑d. Both stated applications match after asserting zero measure/non-top.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M012/0/sources/M012\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/12/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/11\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:123-124\"]},\"M013\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full signature requires a FunLike outer-measure class, and subset inclusion; the statement correctly says an outer measure. Application identifies Lebesgue volume and the interval inclusion.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M013/0/sources/M013\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/13/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/9\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/OuterMeasure/Basic.lean:51-54\"]},\"M014\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Official theorem requires extended metric, measurable and Borel structures, set, NNReal d and measure exactly top, yielding ↑d≤dimH. The slicing argument's stated application matches.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M014/0/sources/M014\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/14/source/signature\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/10\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:126-128\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"One inference R001 is the sole producer of P and its listed inputs are accepted-source kinds; there is no dangling internal graph node. Nevertheless the producer output does not state the full target. Definitions/locals also contain existence and substantive facts asserted as definitions (notably J_i is selected with a covering/length property, and ν definition appends a mass calculation). S001/S002/S003 are argument segments within this single R and are not independent accepted proofs; their assertions must be supported by the complete argument. The supplied task excludes per-inference packet replay, which is not represented here as performed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0\",\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/13\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/22\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions/P\",\"spec.json:/full_target\"],\"finding\":\"Output statement omits the universal binders and hypotheses/domain/metric conventions of the full target; therefore the producer's output is not exactly the specified theorem.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/13\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"J_i is declared as a definition that already chooses an open interval containing B_i with a prescribed length bound. This carries a nontrivial existence/construction assertion without a separate proof or legitimate witness basis; a definition cannot supply it.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals/9\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"The ν definition includes the theorem-like calculation ν(R)=volume([0,1])=1, rather than defining ν alone and deriving its mass from M011 and the restriction definition.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\"],\"finding\":\"The application of the slicing inequality to arbitrary δ-cover is not justified in the argument: C_s(E,δ) is an infimum of sums over countable covers, whereas the sets A_i obtained by slicing at t must be shown to form an admissible cover with the requisite scale and their costs bounded by the corresponding indicators. The text asserts this pointwise but does not fully formalize the dependence of the admissible cover on t or the infimum comparison. This is a missing proof step in the displayed NL0 argument.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","paramete